# Cross-platform line endings.
#
# Shell and Python entry points must stay LF. A trailing CR is invisible on
# Windows but fatal on Unix checkouts: it becomes part of the shebang
# (`#!/usr/bin/env python3\r`) and part of shell option names
# (`set: pipefail\r: invalid option name`). Marking them `eol=lf` keeps every
# checkout byte-identical regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Extensionless shell entry point, and a data file read by shell loops where a
# stray CR would be swallowed into each value.
scripts/zj-git text eol=lf
scripts/zagentic-skills-list text eol=lf
